# Stop the device dying when it tries to enter kernel suspend.
#
# Symptom: "PowerManagerService: Going to sleep due to timeout", then silence,
# then the watchdog reboots. No pstore and no bootreason on this kernel, so
# nothing is recoverable after the fact - it hangs below the framework.
#
# The stock unit never hits this. Comparing kernel wakelocks on both:
#
#   stock (8.1) : PowerManagerService.WakeLocks  pvrservice.platform
#   port  (10)  : (none)
#
# Pico's pvrservice holds a kernel wakelock the whole time it runs, so the stock
# firmware never enters suspend - "sleep" there is display-off only. Our
# pvrservice does not hold it consistently under Android 10, nothing else blocks
# suspend, and the device walks into a path the vendor never exercises.
#
# Take the wakelock ourselves and match the stock behaviour. This is better than
# `svc power stayon true`, which was the stopgap: that forces the SCREEN to stay
# on and is lost on every reboot. This lets the display sleep normally and only
# prevents the kernel suspend that breaks.
#
# Cost: no deep sleep, so idle battery drain is higher. That is exactly the
# tradeoff stock already makes. Proper fix is finding which driver hangs in
# suspend, which needs a working pstore or a serial console.

on boot
    write /sys/power/wake_lock pn2_nosuspend
